  "id": "bambu-x2d",
  "name": "Bambu Lab X2D (both nozzles; stock quick-swap hotends and ducts)",
  "provenance": "X2D dual-nozzle toolhead (gear-and-trigger nozzle change, https://forum.bambulab.com/t/xcellence-made-simple-the-x2d-is-here/249117). Idle hotend modelled on both sides for either active nozzle. Nozzle spacing 20.5 mm from extruder_printable_area (0..256 vs 20.5..256) in the BambuStudio X2D preset (https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/tree/master/resources/profiles/BBL/machine); idle tip held at the 4 mm nozzle_height floor. Nozzle: tip bands of the Bambu quick-swap hotend (0.6 mm land, 35-degree cone capped at 2 mm radius, from https://www.printables.com/model/533213 Hotend.STEP as in bambu-a1), clipped at the BambuStudio nozzle_height floor; Bambu's FAQ says this nozzle family is shared by H2D and P2S (https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/p2s/manual/p2s-faq) and its High Flow hotend is sold for H2/P2S (https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/bambu-high-flow-hotend-h2-p2s). extruder_clearance_height_to_rod 32.8, dist_to_rod 33 (common), max_radius 60 -> gantry underside Z 32.8, symmetric Y span +-33. Housing: X-series layout of bambu-p1s widened by 10.25 mm (half the nozzle spacing) each side. Body boxes are estimates from Bambu wiki/store toolhead photos with the BambuStudio clearances as hard anchors; axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Derived 2026-11-11; calibrated=false.",
